to be strict  "forever", and I (and other good teachers of R)
have taught our students to prefer this in 'serious' code
(i.e., outside of tinkering in the R console) "forever".

And really, as I tried to say in my first e-mail, I don't think
it is a good idea to add such an option:

For consistency, it should apply to *all* uses of  <obj>$<comp> 
not just in the case of data frame <obj>, or if only used for
data frame this becomes somewhat of an inconsistency of using
`$` in R  .....

And then, for more consistency, it should also apply to

 <obj>$<comp>  <- value       i.e., to the `$<-` generic function  (and its methods)

and for that case you'd get zillions of warnings, because it is
very common to add not-yet-existing list components that way;
consequently you'd want one more inconsistency in the use of `$` .

All these reasons would speak strongly against such an option
(yes, even only as option) for me.


